WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.300
Remember when TV networks basically took the
summer off?

00:00:03.760 --> 00:00:05.580
Netflix would never do that to you.

00:00:05.580 --> 00:00:09.470
Like every other month, all year round, the
streaming service will refresh in July with

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:13.060
an impressive batch of original titles and
blockbuster movies.

00:00:13.440 --> 00:00:16.900
Let's start with the streaming giant's own
crop of films and series ...

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:18.480
Friends from College

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.400
Life doesn't get any easier after you earn
that undergraduate degree.

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:27.400
In the comedy series Friends from College,
six college pals reunite in their mid-forties

00:00:27.420 --> 00:00:32.480
and learn something no professor can teach:
friendship and adulthood are way more complicated

00:00:32.480 --> 00:00:33.480
than they realized.

00:00:33.480 --> 00:00:34.480
"It's the middle of the week.

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:35.480
We're not doing drugs.

00:00:35.480 --> 00:00:36.160
Not at my age.

00:00:36.160 --> 00:00:36.800
Not at our age.

00:00:37.580 --> 00:00:42.000
While it's a comedy, the trailer shows that
the series will also have a strong emotional

00:00:42.340 --> 00:00:46.800
core—which isn't all that surprising: Friends
from College comes from creator Nicholas Stoller,

00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:51.200
the director of Forgetting Sarah Marshall
and other comedies that have a lot of heart

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.240
to go with the laughs.

00:00:52.760 --> 00:00:56.860
Stoller directed all eight episodes of the
first season of Friends from College, which

00:00:56.860 --> 00:00:58.440
drops July 14th.

00:00:59.140 --> 00:01:00.060
Castlevania

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:05.140
The classic Nintendo ghoul-whipping video
game has come a long way since its 8-bit origins.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:10.200
Now, for the first time ever, the horror-inspired
backstory of the long running game series

00:01:10.200 --> 00:01:11.620
will make its way to TV.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:17.680
Loosely based on the 1989 game Castlevania
III: Dracula's Curse, Castlevania follows

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:22.500
the last surviving member of the disgraced
Belmont clan on his quest to save Eastern

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:24.800
Europe from the villainous Vlad the Impaler.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:30.140
The trailer looks scary good; we'll find out
for sure when Season 1 arrives on July 7th.

00:01:30.700 --> 00:01:31.400
Ozark

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:37.380
In a stark departure from Arrested Development,
Jason Bateman takes the lead in Ozark, a dark

00:01:37.380 --> 00:01:40.300
drama from the same studio behind House of
Cards.

00:01:40.650 --> 00:01:45.600
Bateman stars as an embattled father who finds
himself dangerously in debt to a powerful

00:01:45.600 --> 00:01:46.980
and ruthless drug lord.

00:01:47.430 --> 00:01:51.820
In an attempt to escape, he moves his wife,
played by Laura Linney, and their two kids

00:01:51.820 --> 00:01:56.460
from the suburbs of Chicago to a summer resort
community in the Missouri Ozarks.

00:01:56.700 --> 00:02:01.240
Bateman also directs and executive produces
the series, which looks like Breaking Bad

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.180
meets Bloodline.

00:02:02.440 --> 00:02:05.640
The 10-episode first season premieres July
21st.

00:02:06.320 --> 00:02:07.060
To the Bone

00:02:07.740 --> 00:02:12.800
Lily Collins stars as an unruly 20-year-old
anorexic girl sent to a group home in To the

00:02:12.800 --> 00:02:17.420
Bone, a bittersweet film Netflix picked up
at the Sundance Film Festival earlier this

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:17.920
year.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:24.060
"People say they love you, but what they mean
is they love how loving you makes them feel

00:02:24.060 --> 00:02:24.920
about themselves."

00:02:25.220 --> 00:02:29.560
Collins is already earning acclaim for her
performance; she's joined in the cast by Keanu

00:02:29.700 --> 00:02:31.240
Reeves and Lili Taylor.

00:02:31.620 --> 00:02:33.680
To the Bone debuts July 14th.

00:02:34.360 --> 00:02:35.340
Chasing Coral

00:02:35.760 --> 00:02:39.959
If you're still on the fence about climate
change and its potentially catastrophic effects,

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.700
this critically acclaimed documentary wants
to sway you.

00:02:43.040 --> 00:02:47.400
The winner of this year's Audience Award for
documentaries at the Sundance Film Festival,

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.931
Chasing Coral centers on the destruction of
coral reefs due to drastic changes in the

00:02:51.940 --> 00:02:52.820
world's temperature.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.560
Look for the doc when it premieres July 14th.

00:02:55.960 --> 00:02:57.740
Ari Shaffir: Double Negative

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:03.540
A stand-up special from comedian and podcast
host Ari Shaffir taped last November at Cap

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:09.060
City Comedy Club in Austin, Texas, Double
Negative is a rare two-parter: The first hour-long

00:03:09.060 --> 00:03:13.670
installment focuses on comedy about kids,
while the second part will focus on the life

00:03:13.670 --> 00:03:16.170
you can't have if you marry and have kids.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:17.849
Both parts drop on July 18th.

00:03:17.849 --> 00:03:19.440
And speaking of comedians...

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:21.180
The Standups

00:03:21.420 --> 00:03:26.780
Netflix has put an increased emphasis on big-name
comedy specials in recent years, and now the

00:03:26.800 --> 00:03:30.400
streaming service is shining the spotlight
on a batch of lesser-known names.

00:03:30.880 --> 00:03:35.430
The first season of The Standups features
six half-hour specials dedicated to some of

00:03:35.430 --> 00:03:37.560
the brightest rising stars in comedy.

00:03:37.560 --> 00:03:39.440
Check the series out on July 4th.

00:03:40.100 --> 00:03:41.220
The Worst Witch

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:46.940
13-year-old British actress Bella Ramsey stars
in The Worst Witch, the latest adaptation

00:03:46.940 --> 00:03:51.100
of Jill Murphy's hugely popular children's
book series from the 1970s.

00:03:51.310 --> 00:03:56.280
Ramsey plays Mildred Hubble, a bumbling young
witch at Cackle's Academy, a school for magic.

00:03:56.300 --> 00:04:00.900
However, she wasn't actually born into a family
of witches, making her an outsider.

00:04:01.160 --> 00:04:06.500
Originally airing on the BBC, the first season
premieres on Netflix on July 21st.

00:04:07.020 --> 00:04:08.640
The Incredible Jessica James

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:14.420
A vehicle for charming former Daily Show correspondent
Jessica Williams, The Incredible Jessica James

00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:18.790
is a thoroughly Millennial romantic comedy
about a young, aspiring playwright in New

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:22.289
York City who's still getting over a recent
breakup.

00:04:22.289 --> 00:04:26.020
Netflix snagged the movie after a bidding
war following a screening on the first day

00:04:26.020 --> 00:04:28.400
of this year's Sundance Film Festival.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:31.160
The film will be ready for streaming on July
28th.

00:04:31.840 --> 00:04:32.800
New Movies

00:04:33.160 --> 00:04:37.620
Plenty of great flicks hit the streaming service
in July, including the well-received prequel

00:04:37.620 --> 00:04:41.520
juggernaut Star Wars: Rogue One, which hits
Netflix July 18th.

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:46.340
It doesn't get much more dramatic than Titanic,
James Cameron's world conquering mega-blockbuster.

00:04:46.740 --> 00:04:49.880
Look for it July 1st, but don't watch it during
your luxury cruise.

00:04:50.240 --> 00:04:55.400
On July 9th, Netflix will add another widely
acclaimed — but much smaller scale — drama:

00:04:55.400 --> 00:05:00.750
2016's Lion, the Oscar-nominated true story
of a man who uses Google Earth to find his

00:05:00.750 --> 00:05:03.080
way back home after being lost as a child.

00:05:03.610 --> 00:05:08.180
If you're looking for laugh, Christopher Guest's
hilarious dog show mockumentary Best in Show

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:10.040
is available July 1st.

00:05:11.380 --> 00:05:13.600
"Yeah, we both have so much in common.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:15.360
We both love soup."

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:21.160
You could also embrace Christmas in July with
Billy Bob Thornton in Bad Santa 2, available

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:21.780
July 8th.

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:26.640
With the kids out of school, Netflix is giving
parents a lot of classic options for summer

00:05:26.640 --> 00:05:27.140
viewing.

00:05:27.620 --> 00:05:32.720
You can start with Steven Spielberg's E.T.:
The Extra-Terrestrial, available July 1st.

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:37.349
If the kids are craving a movie marathon,
the first three films in the prehistoric Land

00:05:37.349 --> 00:05:40.420
Before Time franchise will also be available
the same day.

00:05:40.680 --> 00:05:44.860
After the kids are asleep, check out Here
Alone, a zombie flick about a young woman

00:05:44.940 --> 00:05:50.340
who's forced deep into the woods after a mysterious
epidemic wipes out most of society.

00:05:50.520 --> 00:05:52.200
It's also available July 1st.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:56.980
Starting July 6th, you can also stream The
Void, a sci-fi horror film that follows a

00:05:57.000 --> 00:06:01.360
group of people trapped in a hospital crawling
with grotesque creatures.

00:06:01.580 --> 00:06:07.419
If that's all a little too frightening, starting
July 1st, you can try Taking Lives, an underrated

00:06:07.420 --> 00:06:12.020
2004 psychological thriller starring Angelina
Jolie and Ethan Hawke.

00:06:12.740 --> 00:06:13.700
New TV

00:06:14.180 --> 00:06:17.979
If you're craving a binge this summer, you
could do a whole lot worse than the third

00:06:17.979 --> 00:06:23.250
season of the CW's iZombie, about a young
zombie who needs brains to keep her true self

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:26.039
at bay — and to help the police solve murders.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:27.040
Check it out July 5th.

00:06:27.520 --> 00:06:31.780
If brain munching murder mysteries just aren't
your thing, new episodes of the zombie-free

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:35.720
teen mystery thriller Pretty Little Liars
hit the service on July 20th.

00:06:36.020 --> 00:06:41.060
And if you're more of a basic cable reality
show type binger, Season 4 of the car customizing

00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:44.360
hit West Coast Customs is available July 15th.

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:49.000
With all new things to watch on Netflix, we
can almost forgive them for dropping the first

00:06:49.000 --> 00:06:50.460
six seasons of Futurama.

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:51.240
Almost.

00:06:51.740 --> 00:06:54.660
"If anyone needs me, I'll be in the angry
dome!"

00:06:55.360 --> 00:06:56.520
Thanks for watching!

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.270
Click the Looper icon to subscribe to our
YouTube channel.

00:06:59.270 --> 00:07:01.689
Plus check out all this cool stuff we know
you'll love, too!

